   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `fieldnotes delete INDEX`, and `python tools/check.py` now passes.\n\n**Red:** Before any implementation, the run showed 1 failure and 2 errors. `store.delete` didn't exist (`AttributeError`), and the CLI returned 2 for `delete`.\n\n**Green:** With the implementation in, all 5 tests pass and the line-length check reports nothing. The `exit=0` in my last command came from `tail`, not `check.py`, so I'm relying on the \"OK\" output rather than the exit code.\n\n**Changes**\n- `tests/test_store.py` has four new tests:\n  - Deleting by index removes the right note.\n  - Out-of-range indexes (0, 2 and -1 on a one-note store) raise `IndexError` and leave the notes alone.\n  - The CLI deletes the note and prints `deleted: a`.\n  - The CLI returns exit code 2 for a bad, non-numeric or missing index.\n- `fieldnotes/store.py` has a new `delete(index)`. I also pulled the file write into a `_save` helper that `add` now uses too.\n- `fieldnotes/cli.py` handles `delete INDEX`, and the usage text now lists it.\n\nI made `INDEX` 1-based, in the order `list` prints notes. `list` doesn't print numbers today, so users have to count lines to find an index. If you'd like, I can make `list` number its output, or switch to 0-based indexing. I left both alone because you didn't ask for them.",
