   "reply": "I added a `count` command that prints the number of notes, and the project checks now pass: all 7 tests are green and the line-length rule is clean.\n\n- **Command:** `count` in `fieldnotes/cli.py` prints `len(store.load())`. I also added it to the usage string.\n- **Tests:** a new `CliCountTests` class in `tests/test_store.py` checks the output is `0` with no notes and `2` after adding two.\n- **Docstring:** my first edit pushed the module docstring in `cli.py` over the 100-character limit and failed the check. I shortened it to `add|list|count|delete`, which drops the `TEXT` and `INDEX` argument hints from the docstring. The usage string still has them.\n- **Running the checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set, so I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a fresh temp directory: `NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" python tools/check.py`.",
